5302	Anchorstone Harbor's Request
5303	Defeat 20 murklings on the wharves
5304	A Mender who rode the Windway. News from the windmill isles got here faster than the gulls.
5305	This is Anchorstone Harbor. Since the wind stopped, not one airship has flown. The wharves are crawling with salt flufflings and anchor crabs.
5306	Clear out twenty first, so the porters can get back on the wharves.
5307	Cart wheels rattling on the wharves again. Thank you.
5308	The Rope Bridge
5309	Collect 4 Rope Coils from Barnacle Nestkeepers and tie the rope bridge east of Central Wharf
5310	There was a rope bridge from Central Wharf to Rope Ferry. It snapped the day the Rusty Airship cut its anchor rope and rose.
5311	Barnacle Nestkeepers nest on every wharf, holding rope coils. Four coils and we can tie the bridge again.
5312	The rope bridge is up again! Beyond it: Rope Ferry, Barnacle Shallows… and Rusty Dock.
5313	That's where the airship floats. Keep an eye on the sky.
5314	Crab Chase
5315	Defeat 12 Anchor Crabs
5316	It's Solbaram. I followed you here! Seen the anchor crabs? They used to be gentle, just collecting broken anchors.
5317	With the wind gone, they swing their claws at people. Back off when a round marker shows on the ground. Let twelve of them rest.
5318	Thank you. The sea breeze smells salty again. Here's a ring I found.
5319	Salt Quenching
5320	Bring 5 Salt Crystals
5321	I'm Saltiron, the harbor smith. I've heard about Musoe and Pulmu.
5322	Quench iron in sea salt and it never rusts. Salt flufflings and barnacle pods carry salt crystals. Five, please.
5323	Good, that's a whole year of quenching. For your trouble, a blessed whetstone and blessed glue.
5324	The Airship over Rusty Dock
5325	Bring down the Rusty Airship over Rusty Dock and touch the dock's Pinwheel Beacon
5326	The Rusty Airship hovers over the dock, blocking all wind into the harbor.
5327	It fires its broadside all at once, scattering round markers on the ground, and drops its anchor. It calls gull flocks too.
5328	When enraged, it passes overhead dropping bombs in a line. When the markers form a line, step aside.
5329	…Wind! The moored airships' sails are filling!